  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA consisting of NNN **distinct** positive integers.\n\nFind the **smallest** positive integer ddd such that there exists **no** pair of integers (i,j)(i, j)(i,j) (1≤i&lt;j≤N)(1\\le i\\lt j \\le N)(1≤i&lt;j≤N) where abs(Ai−Aj)abs(A_i - A_j)abs(Ai​−Aj​) is divisible by ddd.\n\nIn other words, d∤abs(Ai−Aj)d \\nmid abs(A_i - A_j)d∤abs(Ai​−Aj​) for all (1≤i&lt;j≤N)(1\\le i \\lt j\\le N)(1≤i&lt;j≤N).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains an integers NNN — the number of the array AAA.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated distinct integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots , A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ denoting the array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the smallest positive integer ddd such that d∤(Ai−Aj)d \\nmid (A_i - A_j)d∤(Ai​−Aj​) for all (1≤i&lt;j≤N)(1\\le i \\lt j\\le N)(1≤i&lt;j≤N).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤2⋅1051 \\leq A_i \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^51≤Ai​≤2⋅105",
      "The sums of&nbsp;NNN and max(A)max(A)max(A) over all test cases does not exceed 3⋅1053 \\cdot 10 ^ 53⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3\n1 2 3\n3\n1 2 10\n3\n1 3 10",
        "output": "3\n5\n4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The possible differences are abs(A1−A2)=1,abs(A1−A3)=2,abs(A2−A3)=1abs(A_1 - A_2) = 1, abs(A_1 - A_3) = 2, abs(A_2 - A_3) = 1abs(A1​−A2​)=1,abs(A1​−A3​)=2,abs(A2​−A3​)=1. The smallest positive integer not dividing any of these differences is 333.\nTest case 222: The possible differences are abs(A1−A2)=1,abs(A1−A3)=9,abs(A2−A3)=8abs(A_1 - A_2) = 1, abs(A_1 - A_3) = 9, abs(A_2 - A_3) = 8abs(A1​−A2​)=1,abs(A1​−A3​)=9,abs(A2​−A3​)=8. The smallest positive integer not dividing any of these differences is 555.\nTest case 333: The possible differences are abs(A1−A2)=2,abs(A1−A3)=9,abs(A2−A3)=7abs(A_1 - A_2) = 2, abs(A_1 - A_3) = 9, abs(A_2 - A_3) = 7abs(A1​−A2​)=2,abs(A1​−A3​)=9,abs(A2​−A3​)=7. The smallest positive integer not dividing any of these differences is 444."
      }
